  "description": {
    "summary": "Catenoid is a minimal surface, given by a parametrisation, genus 0, 2 ends, embedded, with a continuous symmetry group.",
    "source": "curated",
    "curated": "Hang a chain between two points and it settles into a catenary. Spin that curve about the axis between them and you get the catenoid -- the shape a soap film takes when it spans two parallel rings. It was the first minimal surface found after the plane, and apart from the plane it is the only one that is also a surface of revolution. Pull the rings too far apart and the film has no stable shape left to take, and it snaps.",
